   "setup_says": [
    "[ok] unified memory: the experts are read from the model files in place (--mmap-experts), so the GPU's cache holds them instead of a second copy in RAM",
    "[ok] prompt chunk 32,768 (--prefill auto:32768), the draft layer as 4-bit copies (--mtp-q4 all) and one norm per hyper-connection stream in it (--mtp-hnorm stream): measured faster on this part, the answers are unchanged",
    "Tip: for English or code only, --draft-vocab en measured +3.1% decode on this part (the default keeps Chinese, Japanese and Korean drafts).",
    "[ok] 128 GB of RAM: the 29 GB n-gram table is kept in RAM (--ple-io ram), so a new prompt does not wait for its rows from the SSD (a 4K prompt about 18% sooner on a fast card); remove --ple-io ram from the config's args to read it from the SSD instead",
    "[ok] KV streaming on: the context's KV cache lives in RAM (1.8 GB), more experts fit in VRAM"
   ]
